    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d225">

                <pb facs="0261" n="145" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/986.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Kineo, Me.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 7, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The French Minister at Peking has been instructed that the French Government
                    consider the best means of obtaining consent of China to proposed conditions is
                    to suspend any advance. The British Minister has been similarly instructed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mitchell Innes.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
